04bda65b96e2475b9411e65a04d86e359f7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 2:25PM MDT until October 23 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...The Flood Warning is cancelled for a portion of south\ncentral Colorado, including the following areas, Mineral and Rio\nGrande.\n\nThe heavy rain has ended. Please continue to heed remaining road\nclosures.\n\nA Flood Watch remains in effect until 600 PM MDT Friday for a portion\nof south central Colorado...\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache, Central Mineral and Western Rio\nGrande Counties...\n\n* WHEN...Until 500 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Several structures are flooded and evacuations have\noccurred from Wolf Creek Ranch to Fun Valley. Some roads remain\nclosed due to flooding including highway 160 and FR380. The Park\nCreek bridge has been washed away with considerable debris in the\nwater.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 223 PM MDT, Stream gauges indicate flooding continues for the\nSouth Fork Rio Grande, Rio Grande between South Fork and Del\nNorte, and other area streams.\n- The South Fork Rio Grande and other area streams are past their\ncrests and are continuing to fall. The South Fork Rio Grande is\nexpected to fall back below Flood Stage late Friday night.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDel Norte, South Fork, Wagon Wheel Gap and Creede.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 6:50AM MDT until October 25 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...Forecast flooding changed from Minor to Moderate severity for the\nfollowing rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\n.Heavy rainfall across the eastern San Juan mountains and the upper\nRio Grande will cause high flows with moderate flooding expected at\nDel Norte late this morning. The flood crest is expected to reach\n6.60 feet, which is just below a previous record flood crest of 6.80\nfeet.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte...Moderate\nflooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 6.5 feet, Moderate Flood. Water flows over low spots\nin Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. Water threatens homes and RV\npark near Del Norte Park in Del Norte. Homes near First Street and\nthe Oak Street Bridge on Colorado Highway 112 are threatened by\nhigh water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:31 AM MDT Friday the stage was 6.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:31 AM MDT Friday was 6.3 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 6.6 feet\nthis afternoon. It will then fall below flood stage early\ntomorrow afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 6.4\nfeet on 06/29/1927.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e1a5d200d193d27254ad486dd3f82c18f1f81130.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e1a5d200d193d27254ad486dd3f82c18f1f81130.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T19:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231917 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 117 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain threat will develop over the eastern plains on Saturday into Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks Saturday afternoon and evening. - Mainly dry this upcoming week then another storm possible next weekend. && .SHORT TERM /THRO","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000